def max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr, i, k):
    # Base case: If k is less than or equal to i, return the sum of the subsequence from the start to i
    if k <= i:
        return sum(arr[:i+1])

    # If k is greater than i, find the maximum sum including the kth element
    max_sum = max(max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr, j, k-1) + arr[k] for j in range(i+1))

    return max_sum
```

